Subject: config.sub: accept substrate as an OS name

Mirror the binutils patch — wire substrate* into the generic OS pattern so triples like i386-unknown-substrate are recognised at configure time.

---
diff --git a/config.sub b/config.sub
--- a/config.sub	2026-05-11 23:07:23.253167860 -0500
+++ b/config.sub	2026-05-11 23:07:38.939892915 -0500
@@ -1749,7 +1749,7 @@
 	     | onefs* | tirtos* | phoenix* | fuchsia* | redox* | bme* \
 	     | midnightbsd* | amdhsa* | unleashed* | emscripten* | wasi* \
 	     | nsk* | powerunix* | genode* | zvmoe* | qnx* | emx* | zephyr* \
-	     | fiwix* )
+	     | fiwix* | substrate* )
 		;;
 	# This one is extra strict with allowed versions
 	sco3.2v2 | sco3.2v[4-9]* | sco5v6*)
